{"parentUuid":"88a01b23-7cfb-4377-aaba-8fa31d2cc625","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgERHPBNp5LKs7zRTxU76","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"CI is starting on the new tips. Cleaning up the local record of the old SHAs in the plan doc isn't needed, so I'm done here.\n\nAll 17 previously unsigned commits are now signed and force-pushed. They sit on 16 branches, and GitHub shows all 17 as verified.\n\n- **Content unchanged:** each new commit has the same tree, author, date and message as the one it replaces. The stack parents point at the new signed commits.\n- **PRs intact:** all 16 PRs are still open with the same base branches. CI is queued on the new tips and hasn't finished.\n- **Local state:** the local branches and clean worktrees now match the new tips. The `callisto-codex-review-main` and other older worktrees weren't touched.\n- **Cause:** I added `-c commit.gpgsign=false` to the commit commands. That is fixed, and I commit with plain `git commit` from here on.\n- **Not checked:** I didn't verify that the native stack links between PRs survived the force-push. Their bases are unchanged, and I can run `gh stack` if you want to see them.\n- **Not changed:** your `main` and `stack/docs-v1` commits were never affected.\n\nOnce CI is green on the new SHAs, they're ready to merge. The earlier suggestion still stands: stack #267 on #266, since those two conflict on one test file.\n\nresult: All 17 unsigned commits across the 16 PR branches are re-signed with identical content, force-pushed, and show as verified on GitHub; CI is re-running on the new tips."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":994,"cache_read_input_tokens":109017,"output_tokens":501,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","ca