{"parentUuid":"bcd5178d-c00f-4ed0-88bf-a2be2da535c4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEmQH82h3ZdfT8FbRDYN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SqPL24Wj4EH9Lt3MB8FFE8","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c/scratchpad; /usr/bin/git add -A && /usr/bin/git commit -q -m \"fix(identity): reject the colon form of package references\" -m \"A package written \\`cargo:foo\\` is rejected with E316 naming \\`cargo/foo\\` in \\`--package\\`, changeset entries, \\`pre.json\\` keys, group members, package rules, and the product and artifact packages. A group member that fails to resolve no longer hides E316 or E103 behind the missing-member error.\" && /usr/bin/git log -1 '--format=%h %G? %s' && /usr/bin/git push -q -u origin fix/reject-colon-references 2>&1 | tail -2; cat > $S/pr_colon.md <<'EOF'\nA package written with a colon, such as `cargo:foo`, is now rejected with E316 naming the slash form, `cargo/foo`. Bare names and the slash form work as before.\n\n- Applies to `--package` on `add`, `matrix` and `release`, changeset entries, `pre.json` keys, group members, `[[package]]` and `[[package-set]]` `match`, `product-package` and `[[release.artifact]] package`.\n- Group resolution no longer turns every resolver error into the missing-member error, so E103 and E316 reach the user.\n- The ambiguous-dependency warning now lists candidates as `cargo/foo`, the form it accepts.\n- `PackageId::parse` still reads the colon form for internal use; every input surface checks it first through one helper.\n\nThis is the second slice of the canonical-reference work in ADR 12. Canonical-required config (E317), canonical command-line arguments and canonical emission follow.\n\nTests: a rejection test per surface (changeset on `status` and `version`, `add`, `release`, group member, `pre.json`), the existing colon-input tests moved to the slash form, and `just ci` passes.\nEOF\ngh pr create --base main --head fix/reject-colon-references --title \"fix(identity): reject the colon form of package references\" --body-file $S/pr_colon.md 2>&1 | tail -1","description":"Commit signed, push, and open a non-draft PR"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":378,"cache_read_input_tokens":209304,"output_tokens":901,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":378,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":901,"cache_read_input_tokens":209304,"cache_creation_input_tokens":378,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":378},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01SqPL24Wj4EH9Lt3MB8FFE8":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/t06-colon && S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c/scratchpad; /usr/bin/git add -A && /usr/bin/git commit -q -m \"fix(identity): reject the colon form of package references\" -m \"A package written \\`cargo:foo\\` is rejected with E316 naming \\`cargo/foo\\` in \\`--package\\`, changeset entries, \\`pre.json\\` keys, group members, package rules, and the product and artifact packages. A group member that fails to resolve no longer hides E316 or E103 behind the missing-member error.\" && /usr/bin/git log -1 '--format=%h %G? %s' && /usr/bin/git push -q -u origin fix/reject-colon-references 2>&1 | tail -2; cat > $S/pr_colon.md <<'EOF'\nA package written with a colon, such as `cargo:foo`, is now rejected with E316 naming the slas